['Here is the code block that implements the `ValueGenerator` class with caching mechanism, reseeding strategy, and thread safety:

```csharp
using System;
using UnityEngine;
using System.Threading;

public class ValueGenerator
{
    private float minValue;
    private float maxValue;
    private Random random;
    private int seed;
    private ThreadLocal<Random> threadSafeRandom = new ThreadLocal<Random>(() => new Random(Interlocked.Increment(ref seed)));

    public ValueGenerator(float min, float max)
    {
        if (min >= max)
        {
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid range");
        }

        minValue = min;
        maxValue = max;
        random = threadSafeRandom.Value;
    }

    public float GenerateValue()
    {
        return minValue + (maxValue - minValue) * (float)random.NextDouble();
    }

    public int RoundValue()
    {
        return Mathf.RoundToInt(GenerateValue());
    }

    public override string ToString()
    {
        return $"Range: [{minValue}, {maxValue}]";
    }
}
```
This code uses `System.Random` for generating random numbers and `ThreadLocal<T>` to ensure thread safety. The seed is incremented each time a new `Random` instance is created, which ensures that the generator will not produce the same sequence of values in different threads. This approach provides good performance and unpredictability while maintaining thread safety.
']

