            if (buffer_index == BUFFER_SIZE) {
                process_filtered_packets(buffer, buffer_index);
                buffer_index = 0;
            }

            // Add the packet to the buffer
            memcpy(&buffer[buffer_index], &packet, sizeof(Packet));
            ++buffer_index;
        }
    }

    // Process any remaining packets in the buffer
    if (buffer_index > 0) {
        process_filtered_packets(buffer, buffer_index);
    }

    free(buffer);
}
```

This code defines a `Packet` structure and a function pointer type for the filter function. It then allocates a buffer to store filtered packets, processes each packet in the input array, and stores it in the buffer if it passes the filter. If the buffer fills up, it is processed and cleared. After all packets have been processed, any remaining packets in the buffer are processed. Finally, the buffer is freed.

This code does not include error handling for the `malloc` function or the `memcpy` function, which you would need to add based on your specific requirements. It also does not include a definition of the `process_filtered_packets` function, which processes and handles the packets in the buffer.
