['Here is an example of how you might implement this in Java using Spring Boot for microservices architecture, Apache Commons for MD5 hashing, Hystrix for fault tolerance, and Logback for logging. 

```java
import org.apache.commons.codec.digest.DigestUtils;
import com.netflix.hystrix.contrib.javanica.annotation.HystrixCommand;
import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import java.util.concurrent.locks.ReentrantLock;

@Service
public class MD5HashingService {
    private static final Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(MD5HashingService.class);
    private ReentrantLock lock = new ReentrantLock();

    @Autowired
    private ExternalDataStore externalDataStore;

    @HystrixCommand(commandKey = "hashString", fallbackMethod = "fallback")
    public String hashString(String input) throws Exception {
        if (input.length() < 1 || input.length() > 1024) {
            throw new InvalidInputException("Invalid input length");
        }

        lock.lock();
        try {
            return DigestUtils.md5Hex(input);
        } finally {
            lock.unlock();
        }
    }

    public String fallback(String input) {
        logger.error("Fallback method called for input: " + input);
        return null;
    }
}
```

In this example, the `hashString` method is thread-safe due to the use of a ReentrantLock. The lock ensures that only one thread can execute the hashing logic at any given time, preventing contention and improving performance. 

The `@HystrixCommand` annotation is used for fault tolerance. If an error occurs while accessing the external data store, the fallback method will be called to handle the failure gracefully.

For logging, Logback is used with SLF4J as a facade. The logger logs errors and other important information. 

Please note that this is a simplified example and does not include all of the requirements mentioned in your question (e.g., load balancing, configuration management, resource management). You would need to implement these features based on your specific needs and infrastructure.
