import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.locks.ReentrantLock;

public class StreamProcessor {
    private final ReentrantLock lock = new ReentrantLock();
    private Set<Integer> dataSet = new HashSet<>();

    public void processBatch(List<Integer> batch) {
        if (batch == null || batch.isEmpty()) {
            System.out.println("Received empty or null batch");
            return;
        }

        lock.lock();
        try {
            for (int num : batch) {
                // Here you can add your logic to check if the number is already in the set, 
                // and if not, add it. This will be part of Union-Find structure implementation.

                dataSet.add(num);
            }
        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.out.println("Error processing batch: " + e.getMessage());
        } finally {
            lock.unlock();
        }
    }
}
```
This code creates a `StreamProcessor` class that processes batches of integers. It uses a `ReentrantLock` to ensure thread safety, and a `HashSet` to store the data. The `processBatch` method locks the lock before processing each batch, ensuring that only one thread can process a batch at a time.

