['Here's a basic implementation of the `processNetworkStats` function in C using libcsv library. This is a simplified version and does not include all the considerations mentioned above such as integration with an external logging service, memory-mapped files handling, flexible architecture for new data sources, error messages and logging etc.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <csv.h>
#include <math.h>

typedef struct {
    double averageThroughput;
    double stdDeviationLatency;
    double top5PacketLoss[5];
} NetworkStatsSummary;

NetworkStatsSummary processNetworkStats(const char* filename) {
    csv_parser fileParser = CsvParser_new(filename, ",", 1);
    CsvRow* row;

    double throughputSum = 0.0;
    int numRows = 0;
    MinHeap* latencyMinHeap = MinHeap_create();
    NetworkStatsSummary summary;

    while ((row = CsvParser_getRow(fileParser))) {
        const char **rowFields = CsvParser_getFields(row);

        double throughput = atof(rowFields[0]); // Assuming throughput is in the first column
        double latency = atof(rowFields[1]);   // Assuming latency is in the second column
        double packetLoss = atof(rowFields[2]);// Assuming packet loss is in the third column

        throughputSum += throughput;
        MinHeap_insert(latencyMinHeap, latency);
        if (MinHeap_size(latencyMinHeap) > 5) {
            MinHeap_extractMin(latencyMinHeap);
        }

        numRows++;
        CsvParser_destroyRow(row);
    }

    summary.averageThroughput = throughputSum / numRows;

    // Calculate standard deviation of latency using the min-heap
    double sumOfSquares = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < MinHeap_size(latencyMinHeap); ++i) {
        double diff = MinHeap_getItemAtIndex(latencyMinHeap, i) - summary.averageThroughput;
        sumOfSquares += diff * diff;
    }

    summary.stdDeviationLatency = sqrt(sumOfSquares / numRows);

    // Copy top 5 packet loss values from the min-heap
    for (int i = 0; i < MinHeap_size(latencyMinHeap); ++i) {
        summary.top5PacketLoss[i] = MinHeap_getItemAtIndex(latencyMinHeap, i);
    }

    CsvParser_destroy(fileParser);
    return summary;
}
```
This code assumes that the CSV file has three columns: throughput, latency and packet loss. It calculates the average throughput by summing up all values in the first column and dividing by the number of rows. The standard deviation of latency is calculated using a min-heap data structure. Finally, it copies the top 5 packet loss values from the heap to the summary report.

Please note that this code does not handle missing or invalid values, error messages, logging, integration with an external logging service, memory-mapped files handling, flexible architecture for new data sources etc. These are complex topics and would require a more detailed design and implementation.
']

