The code uses a mutex to ensure that only one thread can modify the hash table at a time, preventing race conditions. This is necessary because multiple threads could potentially be trying to add or delete configurations simultaneously.

This implementation assumes that all strings are valid and do not need to be checked for validity. If this were not the case, additional code would be needed to validate these settings.

